  "slug": "crispri-responses-25da",
  "summary": "Two preprints show CRISPRi responses vary by cell line and aging cohort, with proliferation programs confounding rankings and transfer needing partial screening.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is how well CRISPRi perturbation effects generalize beyond the context where they were measured. Perturb-seq of essential genes in four human cell lines gives a median cross-line response correlation of 0.52, and prediction in a new line requires screening about 30% of it. A separate analysis finds that CRISPRi rankings for reversing aging expression signatures change with the aging cohort and track cell growth programs, pointing to proliferation as a confounder. The remaining preprints are methodological and do not concern CRISPRi: cross-modal batch correction, spatial imputation (ARC-Impute) and co-localisation testing (spicyR v2), and sequencing assays (Siphon-seq, Catch*ReSeq, nanopore cell-free RNA extraction comparison).",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
